# Example line for ~/.ssh/authorized_keys.
#
# Give the bridge its own key, used by nothing else. Each option below narrows
# what the key can do. Put everything on ONE line (wrapped here only to read).
# Replace the placeholders:
#   from=         the address or range the device connects from
#   command=      the absolute path to bridge.sh on this machine
#   ssh-ed25519   your device's public key
#   the comment   a label for the device, so you can find the key to revoke it
#
# OpenSSH 7.2 and newer. "restrict" turns off pty, port forwarding, X11
# forwarding and agent forwarding, then command= forces the bridge:
restrict,from="203.0.113.10",command="/home/youruser/voice-to-claude-code-ssh-bridge/bridge.sh" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAExampleKeyReplaceMe phone

# OpenSSH older than 7.2 has no "restrict" keyword. Spell the restrictions out
# instead (one line):
# no-pty,no-port-forwarding,no-X11-forwarding,no-agent-forwarding,no-user-rc,from="203.0.113.10",command="/home/youruser/voice-to-claude-code-ssh-bridge/bridge.sh" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAExampleKeyReplaceMe phone
